raw:
{"thoughts": "Right, Monday the 16th. Saturday was a wipeout: we've only got $840 a week coming in and we paid out $1,821, so the account is empty and the Northgrid bill's still behind, plus the mortgage is overdue to the bank. I hate that. Dave's message is lovely but it's not in writing and it's not a confirmed start date, and I can't keep relying on a 'we'll see'. Lewis's Saturday shift is the one thing I can actually lock down: 6 hours at $10, starting this Saturday. I should confirm it with Lewis properly and say thanks. And I'll chase Dave for the extra hours in writing, politely, since he keeps saying 'sorted' and not putting anything down. The binned bread and grab-and-go tallies are a good excuse to get back to him anyway, because that's useful to him and gives me something to talk about. Food spend is down, so I'll keep an eye on that too, but the real problem is margin, and that means more hours, not fewer bills.",
"acts": [
{"op": "message", "to": "Lewis Pryce", "text": "Lewis, thanks ever so much for sorting the Saturday trial. I'll be in at 9 this Saturday, ready for the 6 hours. Really appreciate you giving me the chance, and let me know if you need anything else from me before then. Maureen"},
{"op": "message", "to": "Dave Royle", "text": "Morning Dave! Thanks for the message. Could you just put the extra bakery hours in writing when you get a chance, with a start date? It makes it easier for me to plan the household money. I've started on the binned bread and grab-and-go tallies, so I'll bring them round to you this week. Hope you're well! Maureen"}
],
"aims": [
"Confirm Lewis's Saturday shift and get paid for it",
"Get Dave to confirm extra hours in writing with a start date",
"Send Dave the binned bread and grab-and-go tallies",
"Rebuild margin in the household account",
"Save toward fishing and fell walking weekends"
]}

{
  "thoughts": "Lewis is off sick and I'm holding the shop — big chance to show I can run it. But I've also got the loan and the rent rise hanging over me, and Sian's a friend, so I should talk to her before it gets worse. First, though, I need to keep the shop ticking over today, and I should get that Dales delivery counted properly on Monday. Maybe I'll price up the food list while I'm at it.",
  "acts": [
    {"op": "converse", "with": "Lewis Pryce", "opening": "Morning Lewis, how's the chest? Just letting you know I've got the shop covered — shelves are getting filled and I'll keep an eye on the queue. Anything specific you want me to watch out for while you're off?"},
    {"op": "message", "to": "Sian Bevan", "text": "Hi Sian, hope you're well. I wanted to catch up about the loan and the rent going up — I'm trying to keep things steady but it's getting tight. Any chance we could have a chat this week about options? Thanks."},
    {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Friday 27 March. Lewis off sick, I'm holding the shop. Need to keep shelves full, queue moving, and count Dales delivery Monday before signing. Also need to sort loan/rent with Sian and build Thursday food list."}
  ],
  "aims": [
    "Run the shop while Lewis is off",
    "Sort loan and rent rise with Sian",
    "Build Thursday food list",
    "Keep household money steady",
    "Monday: count Dales delivery"
  ]
}
